    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick breakdown of the stages for a standard CI/CD pipeline? specifically i need the stages for code commit, automated testing, staging, and production deployment. also just include what kind of gates/checks should be at each stage so we can make sure nothing breaks. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard CI/CD pipeline moves through distinct stages with specific checks. Starting with **Code Commit/Build**, the gate is typically passing unit tests and successful compilation. Next, **Automated Testing** requires passing integration and functional tests before proceeding. The **Staging** environment introduces UAT (User Acceptance Testing) and performance checks to simulate real-world use. Finally, **Production Deployment** usually requires manual approval and runs end-to-end smoke testing post-release to ensure functionality.",
      "source": "target",
