    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. can u go into a bit more detail on the \"gates\" part? like, what are the most common things that cause a pipeline to fail or get blocked at the staging and production stages? i want to make sure we have enough guardrails in place to catch everything before it hits the users.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "At the **Staging** stage, common blockers include failing automated end-to-end tests, performance bottlenecks under load, or discrepancy in environment configurations compared to production. For **Production**, the most critical gates involve security scans (vulnerability checks) failing, or manual sign-off if a business risk threshold is exceeded. Ensuring that monitoring tools are fully integrated and passing basic smoke tests in production acts as a final crucial safeguard.",
      "source": "target",
